    "body": "Use a short worked explanation, a prediction, a purposeful interaction, a debrief, and time to improve the project. Ask “What changed your decision?” and “What would this evidence fail to show?” Teach calculation and interpretation together.\nUse a neutral discovery role-play in Unit 2, a peer usability task in Unit 5, and an observed pilot followed by revision and retest in Unit 7. A classroom task demonstrates performance under those conditions; it is not customer demand or revenue evidence.\nDiscuss formative checks without creating extra uploads. Review five cumulative snapshots. Give actionable feedback before dependent work; a target of five working days must match the actual calendar."
