    "url": "/teaching/ai-solutions/milestone-1.html#main",
    "body": "Decision and communication | 15 | States a testable question, quality boundary, next step, and clear evidence/AI-use disclosure. | Makes the chain from evidence to scope easy to inspect and explains a meaningful revision after discovery. | Strong evidence: 15; Meets the goal: 12; Developing: 7.5; Not demonstrated: 0. Intermediate points within this criterion's maximum are allowed when the instructor explains the criterion-specific evidence. |\n\nHow criterion scores are assigned\n\nEach rubric criterion keeps its published maximum points. The instructor judges\nthe evidence against that criterion's Meets the goal and\nStronger evidence descriptions and uses these numerical anchors.\n\nScoring anchors within each criterion's maximum\nEvidence level | Anchor | What the evidence shows |\n\nStrong evidence | 100% of the criterion maximum | Meets the goal and demonstrates the criterion's stronger evidence or transfer. |\n\nMeets the goal | 80% of the criterion maximum | Demonstrates the stated goal with accurate, usable evidence. |\n\nDeveloping | 50% of the criterion maximum | Shows a relevant attempt, but important evidence is incomplete, unreliable, or needs correction. |\n\nNot demonstrated | 0% of the criterion maximum | Provides no usable evidence for this criterion. |\n\nThese are judgment anchors, not automatic all-or-nothing ratings. Intermediate\npoints are allowed within the criterion maximum, with a comment identifying the\nevidence and remaining gap. For a 25-point criterion the anchors are 25, 20, 12.5\nand 0 points. A defensible decision to narrow, revise, or stop can earn strong\ncredit. These anchors do not change criterion maximums, assessment totals, course\nweights, or previously recorded scores.\n\nA favorable project result is not required; the quality of evidence and judgment matters.\nBefore saving this snapshot\nUser, responsible decision owner, and current process are explicit.\nDiscovery log includes a contrary observation and accurate source labels.\nBaseline table has units, denominators, and interpretation.\nThree alternatives, justified AI capability choice, no-code route, bounded charter, and exclusions are present.\nThe next test and quality boundary are stated; feedback status is clear.\nReturn to the Finish step →"
