    "body": "Explore the lesson here. Canvas holds your check-ins, submissions, feedback, and progress.\nReturn to this lesson\nMilestone 2 · after Unit 5\nFirst usable solution\nA snapshot of the same project record.\nProvide the actual versioned artifact or supervised service kit, its chosen AI capability and operating workflow, three varied bench tests, a brief reviewer access/use check, and a meaningful revision with retest. A document-based service is sufficient when another person can complete the bounded task. A mock-up or demonstration deck alone is not.\nInclude the source card, input/output examples, review criteria, exception handoff, and manual fallback. Identify the permitted input, AI contribution, checked output, and implementation route. A supplied-output route must label its AI step as simulated; do not claim a live model connection or automation. Record assistance honestly. If another person has not attempted the task, show that requirement as pending rather than substituting an invented result.\nMilestone 2 rubricCriterion | Maximum points | Meets the goal | Strong transfer | Scoring anchors |\nUsable end-to-end task | 35 | A reviewer accesses the actual version and completes the bounded task; any assistance and unresolved limitation are recorded. | An unfamiliar reviewer completes a changed input using clear instructions, and the author explains why the design transfers. | Strong evidence: 35; Meets the goal: 28; Developing: 17.5; Not demonstrated: 0. Intermediate points within this criterion's maximum are allowed when the instructor explains the criterion-specific evidence. |\nGrounded AI use and human control | 25 | The chosen capability fits the task; permitted inputs, the AI output, live or simulated execution, reviewer, source boundary, exception, and fallback are explicit and checkable. | Shows a consequential AI error or limitation and an effective correction without relying on the assistant’s self-confidence. | Strong evidence: 25; Meets the goal: 20; Developing: 12.5; Not demonstrated: 0. Intermediate points within this criterion's maximum are allowed when the instructor explains the criterion-specific evidence. |\nTesting, revision, and retest | 25 | Ordinary, incomplete, and exception cases have expected and actual results; a meaningful defect is revised and retested. | Tests whether the change affects another path and explains residual uncertainty or an alternative cause of failure. | Strong evidence: 25; Meets the goal: 20; Developing: 12.5; Not demonstrated: 0. Intermediate points within this criterion's maximum are allowed when the instructor explains the criterion-specific evidence. |"
